# Language switcher 404 fix. VitePress's LangSwitch does *not* strip
# the source locale before prepending the target locale, so clicking
# another language on any verse page produces a broken URL. Mapping
# observed (source page → target URL that needs to resolve):
#
#   /ru/<ru-slug>            + English  →  /en/ru/<ru-slug>
#   /ru/<ru-slug>            + Eesti    →  /et/ru/<ru-slug>
#   /en/<en-slug>            + Русский  →  /<en-slug>
#   /en/<en-slug>            + Eesti    →  /et/<en-slug>
#   /et/<et-slug>            + Русский  →  /<et-slug>
#   /et/<et-slug>            + English  →  /en/<et-slug>
#
# Rewrite each of those to the same book's canonical page in the
# target locale, so readers land on the same verse instead of a 404.
# (Book IV 'devops-samsara' and the colophon share a slug across all
# three locales — no rule needed for those.)

